  <notes>The first word "fus," is a fragment carried over from the previous page and is kept as printed. The marginal references are printed in small type and some are hard to read: "l.52. §.1." and "l.s.11.D." may be "l.52." and "l.5.§.11.D." respectively; both are doubtful. "si quadr." is printed with a long-s form and is read as "si". The catchword "do" completes "quando", which is split across the page end; the main text ends at the hyphenated "quan-".</notes>
